    "congress": 118,
    "constitutionalAuthorityStatementText": "<pre>\n[Congressional Record Volume 169, Number 120 (Thursday, July 13, 2023)]\n[House]\nFrom the Congressional Record Online through the Government Publishing Office [<a href=\"https://www.gpo.gov\">www.gpo.gov</a>]\nBy Ms. MATSUI:\nH.R. 4624.\nCongress has the power to enact this legislation pursuant\nto the following:\nArticle 1, Section 8 of the United States Constitution\nThe single subject of this legislation is:\nTo prohibit the discriminatory use of personal information\nby online platforms in any algorithmic process, to require\ntransparency in the use of algorithmic processes and content\nmoderation, and for other purposes.\n[Page H3576]\n</pre>",
